---
name: cache-parallel
model: openai:gpt-5.6-sol
description: "Test whether out-of-order parallel completion changes model payload order"
reasoning: high
maxSteps: 8
timeout: "3m"
skills:
  auto: false
tools:
  bash:
    timeout: "20s"
    commands:
      - "node benchmarks/cache-input/fixture.mjs *"
---

In one model turn, issue these four Bash calls in the written A-B-C-D order.
They must be sibling tool calls in one response and run in parallel. Do not use
`code_exec` and do not wait between calls.

1. `node benchmarks/cache-input/fixture.mjs --label parallel-a --bytes 4096 --delay 6000`
2. `node benchmarks/cache-input/fixture.mjs --label parallel-b --bytes 4096 --delay 0`
3. `node benchmarks/cache-input/fixture.mjs --label parallel-c --bytes 4096 --delay 3000`
4. `node benchmarks/cache-input/fixture.mjs --label parallel-d --bytes 4096 --delay 1000`

After all four return, make one separate Bash call:
`node benchmarks/cache-input/fixture.mjs --label parallel-marker --bytes 1024 --delay 0`

Do not inspect or restate payloads. Report completion with only the intended
call order: parallel-a, parallel-b, parallel-c, parallel-d, parallel-marker.
